{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xgmeksowt2mhf5sk54jxh3neqec2aehip3m2ir26nfkb7scb5x6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Lu2SEY149LsfGQuLq79fwm","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-qEO2oO/translation/tests/common/mod.rs","old_string":"/// `cargo test` does **not** build the `cdylib` artifact, so if it is absent we\n/// build it on demand. That keeps a bare `cargo test` self-sufficient while\n/// still testing the real `.so` through `dlopen`/`dlsym`.\nfn find_rust_so() -> PathBuf {\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().expect(\"current_exe\");\n    let profile_dir = exe\n        .parent()\n        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n        .expect(\"<target>/<profile>/deps/<exe>\")\n        .to_path_buf();\n    let so = profile_dir.join(\"libdiv_euclid_lib.so\");\n    if so.is_file() {\n        return so;\n    }\n\n    let is_release = profile_dir","new_string":"/// `cargo test` does **not** build (or refresh) the `cdylib` artifact, so we\n/// build it ourselves *unconditionally*. Building only when the file is missing\n/// is not enough: a `.so` left over from an earlier `src/lib.rs` would be\n/// silently tested instead of the current source. `cargo build` is a no-op when\n/// already up to date, so this is cheap.\nfn find_rust_so() -> PathBuf {\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().expect(\"current_exe\");\n    let profile_dir = exe\n        .parent()\n        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n        .expect(\"<target>/<profile>/deps/<exe>\")\n        .to_path_buf();\n    let so = profile_dir.join(\"libdiv_euclid_lib.so\");\n\n    let is_release = profile_dir"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":850,"cache_read_input_tokens":109997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":850,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tie